{"cwd": "/tmp/flyrig-sandboxes/20261127T120505/websearch-tool", "delta": "Claude Code hooks are user-defined shell commands that run at fixed points in the session lifecycle. They're configured in `~/.claude/settings.json` (user) or `.claude/settings.json` (project). Common uses include auto-formatting after edits, blocking risky commands, and notifications. Hooks are deterministic, so they run every time rather than depending on the model to choose to run them. A non-zero exit lets Claude see the failure and adjust. Hook events include PreToolUse and PostToolUse. You can also manage them with `/hooks` in a session.\n\n", "final": false, "hook_event_name": "MessageDisplay", "index": 0, "message_id": "e8e3f77c-11a0-4ddc-88a7-7b759d4642c7", "prompt_id": "b8e93928-007d-4e2e-9b41-2de874338440", "scratchpad_dir": "<SCRATCHPAD_DIR>", "session_id": "<SESSION_ID>", "transcript_path": "<TRANSCRIPT_PATH>", "turn_id": "5d1fa97b-c2fb-4752-a81c-a74200b0128f"}
